ription\": \"Two pieces of SQL folklore, settled with capsules. (1) \\\"Avoid OUTER JOIN \\u2014 it's wasteful; if foreign keys guarantee a match, use INNER.\\\" Tested by sweeping the orphan rate (fraction of child rows whos\",\n      \"path\": \"queue/outer_join_fk.yaml\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"quack_execution_modes\",\n      \"description\": \"Mechanism experiment for the Quack protocol (DuckDB 1.5.3 beta). An earlier exploratory run showed attach-mode protocol overhead GROWS with scan size (2.7x at 100K rows, 4.9x at 1M) even though the an\",\n      \"path\": \"queue/quack_execution_modes.yaml\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"quack_native_vs_adbc\",\n      \"description\": \"Isolates the result-transport CLIENT for DuckDB-over-Quack: identical seeded data, identical SQL, identical Quack server software; the only variable is whether the large result is pulled via the NATIV\",\n      \"path\": \"queue/quack_native_vs_adbc.yaml\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"quack_residual_threads\",\n      \"description\": \"The execution-modes experiment left an open question: pushdown-mode Quack runs the identical query on the identical file ~1.9x slower than in-process DuckDB, and the residual scales with execution wor\",\n      \"path\": \"queue/quack_residual_threads.yaml\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"quack_selectivity\",\n      \"description\": \"Closes the open boundary from the execution-modes study, whose query had no WHERE clause. The selectivity suite filters to a different fraction of rows per query (0.1%\\u201320%). The question: is attach-mo\",\n      \"path\": \"queue/quack_selectivity.yaml\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"quack_vs_duckdb\",\n      \"description\": \"Measures the cost of DuckDB's Quack client-server protocol (beta, v1.5.3) against the same engine running in-process. Identical storage files, identical SQL (the quack engine reuses the duckdb scenari\",\n      \"path\": \"queue/quack_vs_duckdb.yaml\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"